    "name": "Green Garlic",
    "description": "<p>Green garlic (also called young garlic or spring garlic) is simply garlic that hasn't fully matured. Green garlic is pulled from the ground before the clove and bulb skins dry out, so you might see green garlic at various stages of growth: with a barely discernible bulb (like a green onion), with a small bulb, but no clove separation (like a spring onion), or with a large bulb and cloves. Either way is delicious.</p><br /><br />",
